<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Third Republic of Venezuela</h1><p class="st-meta">1817 CE – 1819 CE · capital Angostura</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The patriot republic Bolívar rebuilt from Angostura on the Orinoco, which launched the campaigns that freed northern South America.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After exile in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jamaica">Jamaica</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-empire-of-haiti">Haiti</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Bolívar</a> returned to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/venezuela">Venezuela</a> in 1816. In 1817 patriot forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-piar">Manuel Piar</a> and Bolívar captured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayana-province">Guayana</a> region and its town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciudad-bolivar">Angostura</a>, now Ciudad Bolívar, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orinoco">Orinoco</a>, giving the patriots a secure base. The republic was proclaimed there.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Bolívar</a> consolidated his authority, ordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-piar">Piar</a>'s execution in 1817 for insubordination. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-antonio-paez">José Antonio Páez</a> won over the llaneros of the plains, and British and Irish volunteers formed the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a>. The newspaper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/correo-del-orinoco">Correo del Orinoco</a> spread patriot views from 1818. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-angostura">Congress of Angostura</a> met in February 1819, when Bolívar delivered his famous address on government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Bolívar</a>'s crossing of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andecavi">Andes</a> and victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-boyaca">Boyacá</a> in August 1819, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-angostura">Congress of Angostura</a> proclaimed the union of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/venezuela">Venezuela</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gran-colombia">Gran Colombia</a> in December 1819.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/third-republic-of-venezuela.jpg" alt="Third Republic of Venezuela" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Salvadoroff · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandera_de_la_Tercera_Rep%C3%BAblica_de_Venezuela,_1817-1819.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1817 CE – 1819 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Angostura</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Simón Bolívar, Francisco Antonio Zea</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/venezuela">Venezuela</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tercera República de Venezuela</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1818&amp;focus=third-republic-of-venezuela" aria-label="Third Republic of Venezuela on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2818 1801 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Third Republic of Venezuela lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3138 2057L3156 2042M3138 2057L2945 2261"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3156 2042h0M2945 2261h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3138 2057h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3138 2057h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1818&amp;focus=third-republic-of-venezuela">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
